DTEND:20260811T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T202314Z
UID:5gfemqkcskpc64hohs20dq2hpr@google.com
CREATED:20260901T201716Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><strong>Join us for an open discussion on the BAD1 White Pap
 er with Anna Auerbach\,</strong> lead candidate for Volt Berlin in the Sept
 ember election\, lawyer\, and startup founder.</p><p>​This conversation is 
 particularly exciting because Anna Auerbach brings a unique perspective. As
  both a political leader and a startup founder\, she understands the realit
 ies of building a company firsthand. That combination offers a rare opportu
 nity to discuss how Berlin can become a more founder-friendly city with som
 eone who has experienced the ecosystem from the inside.</p><p>​BAD1 has alw
 ays been about turning ideas into action. Our goal isn't just to publish re
 commendations—it's to make sure they reach the people shaping Berlin's futu
 re. That's why we're inviting all democratic political leaders to discuss t
 he most pressing challenges and opportunities for Berlin's startup ecosyste
 m.</p><p>​What started as a small initiative has grown into an exciting mov
 ement that brings together founders\, investors\, operators\, and ecosystem
  builders around a shared mission: making Berlin the best place in Europe t
 o build ambitious companies.</p><p>​During this session\, we'll present the
  BAD1 White Paper\, discuss its key recommendations\, hear Anna Auerbach's 
 perspective on the future of Berlin as a startup hub\, and open the floor f
 or questions and discussion from the community.</p><p>​Whether you've contr
 ibuted to BAD1 from the beginning or are joining the conversation for the f
 irst time\, we'd love to have you there.</p><p>​<strong>Moderation:</strong
 > Julian Teicke</p><p>​<strong>Agenda:</strong></p><p>​5.15 - 5.30: doors o
 pening<br>5.30 - 6:10: fireside chat<br>6.10 - 6.30: Q&amp\;A</p><p>​<stron
 g>Download the full paper here:</strong>  <a href="https://www.berlinaufdie
 eins.de/BAD1_White_Paper_Berlin.pdf?utm_source=luma" target="_blank">https:
 //www.berlinaufdieeins.de/BAD1_White_Paper_Berlin.pdf</a></p><p>​BAD1 Found
 ing Partners: The Delta\, JUNI\, Dentsu</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T201716Z
LOCATION:The Delta Campus\, Donaustraße 44\, 12043 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:BAD1 & Anna Auerbach (Volt): Shaping the Future of Berlin's Startup
  Ecosystem
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
